  "worked_solution": "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+0y=-8 \\\\ x-3y=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
